---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { rel, SUPPORT_EMAIL, LEGAL_NAME } from '../../consts';
const description = `Privacy policy for SendBrake: Message Check by ${LEGAL_NAME}.`;
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy · SendBrake: Message Check" description={description} path="/privacy/send-brake">
  <main class="page">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:720px;">
      <a class="back" href={rel('/privacy/')}>← All privacy policies</a>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">SendBrake: Message Check · Effective date: September 22, 2026</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        {LEGAL_NAME} operates SendBrake, a free message-decision app supported by ads. It has no account
        or inbox connection and cannot send a message. The default check runs on your iPhone. The optional
        Jev check sends the draft and any note you entered to our Cloudflare proxy and TypeSafe AI only
        after you choose the online check and see its disclosure. Jev returns Send, Rewrite, or Leave unsent;
        it does not write a message for you.
      </p>

      <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The draft and optional note during the active check.</li>
        <li>History containing your decision, optional short label, and dates, but not the draft or note.</li>
        <li>App settings, ad-frequency counters, and the local Remove Ads entitlement state.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The draft and note are cleared after Save, Start over, or backgrounding. The iOS share extension
        can receive text or a URL you explicitly share into SendBrake; it does not connect to your inbox.
        The original text is not saved to history, diagnostics, result cards, or ad requests. Deleting the
        app removes its local history.
      </p>

      <h2>Optional online Jev check</h2>
      <p>
        If you select Check with Jev, SendBrake sends the draft, message-channel choice, and any optional
        note over HTTPS to a Dudley Development Cloudflare Worker. The Worker forwards that input to
        <a href="https://typesafe.ai/legal/privacy-policy">TypeSafe AI</a> for a closed-set decision.
        TypeSafe may retain API input under its policy; do not use this option for text you are unwilling
        to share with that provider. The Worker logs only response status, not the draft or note.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cloudflare supplies the request IP address to the Worker. It is hashed with a server secret for a
        daily abuse-limit counter; the counter does not store the raw IP address or draft. Cloudflare and
        TypeSafe process data under their own privacy terms. If the online service fails or reaches its
        limit, SendBrake labels the on-device fallback instead of presenting it as a Jev result.
      </p>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        Sharing a result uses the iOS share sheet and includes the decision summary you choose, not the
        source draft. The destination you select receives that shared content under its own privacy
        practices; Dudley Development does not receive a copy.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
      <p>
        The free version uses Google AdMob. SendBrake requests non-personalized ads, disables Google's
        publisher first-party identifier, and does not request Apple's tracking permission. It makes no
        ad request in the European Economic Area, United Kingdom, Switzerland, or if it cannot determine
        the device's region. No draft, note, label, or decision is included in an ad request.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where ads are allowed, Google's SDKs may process an IP address, device or app-scoped identifiers,
        coarse location inferred from IP, advertising data, product interactions, impressions, crash data,
        performance data, and other diagnostics to deliver, measure, limit, and protect ads and provide app
        functionality. Google's manifests may declare tracking for Device ID even though this app requests
        non-personalized ads and does not show an Apple tracking-permission prompt. We do not run separate
        PostHog or Sentry services in SendBrake.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">Google's advertising policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>.</li>
        <li>A banner appears only on History; an interstitial may appear only after a natural break, subject to session, time, and daily caps.</li>
        <li>A one-time Remove Ads purchase removes banner and interstitial ads.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        Apple processes the Remove Ads purchase. We do not receive payment-card details. The app checks
        StoreKit for an active entitlement so it can remove ads and restore the purchase.
      </p>

      <h2>Children, changes, and contact</h2>
      <p>
        SendBrake is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect their personal
        information. Material policy changes will appear here with a new effective date before the changed
        practice ships. Questions or privacy requests? Email
        <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
